  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 4 and takes about 1 hour."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Shio"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ramen is the lightest of the four classic ramen styles. The broth is pale and clear, relying on a well-made chicken stock and a salt"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "tare"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "for its depth. On top sits"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "chashu"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "pork, which you can prepare a day ahead to save time on the day."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The tare is what makes shio ramen sing. Mix it separately and add it to each bowl just before ladling in the hot broth. This way every portion is seasoned individually and you can adjust the salt level to taste. Do not add the tare to the whole pot of broth or you lose that control."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
